Finding from k5. _ensure_ca renames ca.key and ca.crt one after the other without a lock: two runs at once or a crash in between can leave a key that does not match the certificate (the -s check passes, every signing fails); a missing ca.key alone silently replaces the root and every device turns foreign-ca. Test CA only, so low. Done when: a lock around creation, key/cert pair checked on load, a lone file is an error instead of a new CA; tests.

